# Vendored DRL content snapshot: pin to LF on every platform.
#
# Why: manifest.json (the integrity seal for _vendored/drl_corpus/) stores a
# sha256 per file computed over the LF bytes that scripts/sync_drl_corpus.py
# copies from the DRL. This repo runs with core.autocrlf=true, so without an
# explicit rule a Windows checkout would smudge these text files to CRLF, whose
# sha256 no longer matches the manifest. The integrity gate
# (tests/test_drl_corpus_vendored.py::test_manifest_sha256_verifies_all_files)
# would then FAIL on a fresh Windows clone even though CI (Linux) passes.
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checked-out bytes deterministic on every platform,
# so the integrity seal is reproducible everywhere. See
# _vendored/drl_corpus/README.md for the full provenance story.
_vendored/drl_corpus/** text eol=lf
